{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/562137-pangea-and-the-ki-en-gir","id":562137,"title":"Pangea and the Ki-En-Gir","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mummy: The Curse"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-06-20T12:48:46-07:00","id":562137,"title":"Pangea and the Ki-En-Gir","content":"So, as of the Dark Eras: Neolithic chapter that we are getting the pre-Sundering Border Marches were surprisingly recent in their existence. They were inhabited by physical entities with the power of great spirits, some of which might be considered gods (among which were Father Wolf). <br /> <br /> The Ki-En-Gir fielded sorcerers who claimed to be one-third divine against the forces of the Shan'iatu. <br /> <br /> Maybe they were on to something about that heritage ... maybe their ancestors mated with the natives of the Border Marches before they collapsed?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-20T12:51:51-07:00","id":562153,"title":"","content":"It sounds very likely when you put it like that, doesn't it?<br /> <br /> Man I love that Neolithic Mage got turned into a Werewolf crossover era.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-20T12:59:49-07:00","id":562162,"title":"","content":"Given that the First Tongue shares intense similarities to Sumerian, it wouldn't surprise me to have some pretty thick ties between Ki-En-Gir and some of the spirit gods. <br /> <br /> We can't forget about the Werewolf god-kings of Bau, either.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-20T15:03:53-07:00","id":562242,"title":"","content":"As odd as this sounds, the Brineborn ought to be iterations more influential and well-known in ancient Sumeria.<br /> <br /> It'd be interesting if this was reflected - would the Forsaken be comfortable with a history which paints them as the inferiors to the FISH SHIFTERS of all folks? But seriously, the Ki En Gir had a vast cultural respect for Brineborn which was serious enough that actual Sumerian religion is largely based upon the idea of fish-people mystics with sagelike powers emerging from the deep.<br /> <br /> I have a question! Are these Border Marches mentioned in other gamelines I'm unfamiliar with, like Changeling or Mage?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3386-piff","name":"Piff","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3386_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"442"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-20T15:19:16-07:00","id":562270,"title":"","content":"As I mentioned in another thread on this forum somewhere, ancient Sumerian piscine sages are already referenced in Werewolf 2e.<br /> <br /> The Border Marches are not generally mentioned in other game lines because they ceased to exist in a meaningful state many millennia ago; that they ever existed at all is important to Werewolf mythos and the spirit world, but most other lines don't have the same interaction with the spirit world in the first place.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-21T15:06:10-07:00","id":563430,"title":"","content":"Free Council mentions the Gauntlet being it's own very weird realm. It's full of weird trilobites that seem to congregate where the Gauntlet is highest. I very much doubt it's meant to be part of a broader cosmology though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-21T16:23:26-07:00","id":563509,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/562137-pangea-and-the-ki-en-gir?p=562162#post562162\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Given that the First Tongue shares intense similarities to Sumerian, it wouldn't surprise me to have some pretty thick ties between Ki-En-Gir and some of the spirit gods.<br /> <br /> We can't forget about the Werewolf god-kings of Bau, either.</div> </div> </div> </div>Bau's not for two thousand more years.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-21T16:33:55-07:00","id":563517,"title":"","content":"True but Ki-En-Gir isn't there yet either.<br /> I'm a little unclear of the exact timing but I thought Ki-En-Gir &amp; Bau were rather close together. A case of couple of centuries at most.<br /> <br /> Still that is a little off topic. I fully support the idea that the 'one third divine' ruler was descendant from a Pangean and had good relations with (if s/he was not) the Brineborn.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-21T16:37:23-07:00","id":563519,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/562137-pangea-and-the-ki-en-gir?p=563430#post563430\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Free Council mentions the Gauntlet being it's own very weird realm. It's full of weird trilobites that seem to congregate where the Gauntlet is highest. I very much doubt it's meant to be part of a broader cosmology though.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That's the hole where the Border Marches, also known as Pangaea, used to exist. Life is still there, in the form of those trilobites.<br /> <br /> Presumably, though rarer, there would be azlu nests. Sort of floating labyrinthine web tunnels full of azlu, both luthazlu and azarath, along with the desiccated remains of eons worth of prey. Or not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 06-21-2015, 07:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-21T16:38:45-07:00","id":563520,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Piff</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/562137-pangea-and-the-ki-en-gir?p=562242#post562242\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As odd as this sounds, the Brineborn ought to be iterations more influential and well-known in ancient Sumeria.<br /> <br /> It'd be interesting if this was reflected - would the Forsaken be comfortable with a history which paints them as the inferiors to the FISH SHIFTERS of all folks? But seriously, the Ki En Gir had a vast cultural respect for Brineborn which was serious enough that actual Sumerian religion is largely based upon the idea of fish-people mystics with sagelike powers emerging from the deep.<br /> <br /> I have a question! Are these Border Marches mentioned in other gamelines I'm unfamiliar with, like Changeling or Mage?</div> </div> </div> </div>My personal headcanon is that the Forsaken had a hostile takeover. The Uratha have been known for killing Brineborn and having a distaste for them, if I remember <i>War Against the Pure</i> correctly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-21T23:33:57-07:00","id":563767,"title":"","content":"Perhaps the sorcerers of Ki En Gir were to the Brineborn what the Wolf-Blooded are to the Uratha. With or without the aid of full-on fish-shifters they could have practiced Rites, and possibly bribed or compelled spirits to aid them against the forces of Irem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","name":"CatDoom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-28T20:16:24-07:00","id":681708,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/562137-pangea-and-the-ki-en-gir?p=563509#post563509\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bau's not for two thousand more years.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You shot who in the what now?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2244-nothri","name":"nothri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-28T20:53:18-07:00","id":681721,"title":"","content":"Okay. Back Step.<br /> <br /> The Dog Kings of Sumer fell to the armies of King Gudea of Lagash, who ruled from 2144 BCE to 2124 BCE. I don't know how long the Forsaken ran as demigods, but going from Gudea's start, it's been 1688 years since the <i>fall</i> of the Nameless Empire. The Bird and the Bull takes place in 5500 BCE, came <i>before</i> the rise of the Empire, and has a distance of 3356 years from when Gudea started his reign.<br /> <br /> Now, how is that relevant?<br /> <br /> No idea. I forgot why I brought that up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-29T10:38:27-07:00","id":682209,"title":"","content":"What if there really <i>were</i> human-spirits at one time, and either the Shan'iatu or Ki--an-Gir (or both) were such. (Maybe the Shan'iatu had consumed most of their kin, become very powerful, but weren't satisfied with their metaphysical condition, wanting to be qualitatively more than spirits, not just a powerful example?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-29T10:47:44-07:00","id":682219,"title":"","content":"What if they went off and stormed the heavens and became supernal symbols of something or other?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-29T10:57:43-07:00","id":682226,"title":"","content":"I find both unlikely, but that's me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-30T07:05:01-07:00","id":683075,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/562137-pangea-and-the-ki-en-gir?p=682219#post682219\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What if they went off and stormed the heavens and became supernal symbols of something or other?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Shan'iatu being humanesque but not human and dissatisfied with that condition is canon, and Hisil-spirit-based heritage is the point of the thread. So an idea to tie the two together isn't unreasonable.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-30T10:03:22-07:00","id":683262,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/562137-pangea-and-the-ki-en-gir?p=681721#post681721\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay. Back Step.<br /> <br /> The Dog Kings of Sumer fell to the armies of King Gudea of Lagash, who ruled from 2144 BCE to 2124 BCE. I don't know how long the Forsaken ran as demigods, but going from Gudea's start, it's been 1688 years since the <i>fall</i> of the Nameless Empire. The Bird and the Bull takes place in 5500 BCE, came <i>before</i> the rise of the Empire, and has a distance of 3356 years from when Gudea started his reign.<br /> <br /> Now, how is that relevant?<br /> <br /> No idea. I forgot why I brought that up.</div> </div> </div> </div>Question: what is the Bird and the Bull? I like to keep up with the WOD but this one is drawing a total blank. <br /> <br /> Also, as far as I know we only have a firm date of 3832 BC for the FALL of the Nameless Empire. I was under the impression that when it arose and how long it lasted were left to the ST.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2244-nothri","name":"nothri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-30T10:14:13-07:00","id":683266,"title":"","content":"The Bird and the Bull is the name of the Neolithic Mage/Werewolf Era in Dark Eras. It's been openly said by Dave to take place before the Shan'iatu built Irem, and it's supported by the fact that Irem arose after the creation of Sothis through the sacrifice of Aset, as mentioned in Book of the Deceived.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 09-30-2015, 01:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-30T10:22:18-07:00","id":683268,"title":"","content":"The Bull and the Bird is now called (as of the last draft I wrote, might get changed again since that) the Sundered World. It does occur before the rise of Irem, but I'm not sure exactly how long before - fine details such as a few millennia here and there, you know <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-30T10:30:27-07:00","id":683271,"title":"","content":"I admit, I liked The Bird and the Bull better. :/<br /> <br /> But yeah, Irem itself was given a sort-of timeline with Book of the Deceived. THe Sundered World just affirms that there's an upper limit to how long it could be.<br /> <br /> Of course, that's ignoring the fact that everything's essentially a toolbox. Mummy less so, but still.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-30T11:07:11-07:00","id":683304,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/562137-pangea-and-the-ki-en-gir?p=682219#post682219\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What if they went off and stormed the heavens and became supernal symbols of something or other?</div> </div> </div> </div>Unfortunately, one of the things the Neolithic Era <i>does</i> have in it, along with the crossover sidebar talking about how the Shan'iatu haven't built Irem yet, is an Exarch.<br /> <br /> It's pre-Sundering, not pre-Fall. The Exarchs already ruled the supernal while the Shan'iatu were building up to their project in the Sahara.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-30T11:31:35-07:00","id":683345,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/562137-pangea-and-the-ki-en-gir?p=683304#post683304\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Unfortunately, one of the things the Neolithic Era <i>does</i> have in it, along with the crossover sidebar talking about how the Shan'iatu haven't built Irem yet, is an Exarch.<br /> <br /> It's pre-Sundering, not pre-Fall. The Exarchs already ruled the supernal while the Shan'iatu were building up to their project in the Sahara.</div> </div> </div> </div>I meant the spirits of humanity, not the Shan'iatu. As far as I can tell there was never any mention of a date when they disappeared, if they ever existed, but they just aren't there. And certainly taking up the thrones of tyranny is a human thing to do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 09-30-2015, 02:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-30T11:37:39-07:00","id":683347,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/562137-pangea-and-the-ki-en-gir?p=683345#post683345\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I meant the spirits of humanity, not the Shan'iatu. As far as I can tell there was never any mention of a date when they disappeared, if they ever existed, but they just aren't there. And certainly taking up the thrones of tyranny is a human thing to do.</div> </div> </div> </div>I read your earlier reply as a dismissal; now I'm wondering if I misunderstood you. Sorry if so.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-30T11:41:28-07:00","id":683349,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/562137-pangea-and-the-ki-en-gir?p=683347#post683347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I read your earlier reply as a dismissal; now I'm wondering if I misunderstood you. Sorry if so.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, it was just another theory.<br /> <br /> I suppose I should have been more clear about who the 'they' were.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 09-30-2015, 02:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-30T13:18:35-07:00","id":683462,"title":"","content":"A quick examination of Book of the Deceived states that Isis (or her equivalent) was killed on the rising of a Sothic Turn, and Irem was erected after &quot;centuries passed&quot;. A quick check on the old calculator puts her death (and therefore Azar's ascension into Duat) at 5293 BCE. Now...consider this...in 5500 according to what I'm seeing in the Open Development the Gauntlet had not yet arisen and Father Wolf was still alive....getting weak but still doing his job. Now isn't it interesting that an act of patricide (Azar's death) takes place right around the time that Father Wolf's children are gonna murder their parent? Isn't it even more interesting that Azar's ascension into the realm of Duat unseats a half-man, half-canine god who's self-declared duty is to guide the worthy souls to the afterlife and make sure the unworthy and other entities do not cross over? <br /> <br /> What am I getting at here? I have no idea. I just think...its interesting that Father Wolf and Anubis both experience a major downfall and cosmic shift within a potentially close span of one another. Could the two be related?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2244-nothri","name":"nothri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-30T13:34:44-07:00","id":683471,"title":"","content":"It's possible. It's also possible it was just a really bad day in the offices of creation.<br /> <br /> Either way, the Ruin must have been cackling.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-30T20:45:20-07:00","id":683858,"title":"","content":"That does have some implications I hadn't thought of before: the Exarchs, at the very least, are Supernal symbols of tyranny and oppression, which is half of what the Deceived temakhs are, at the least","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-30T21:01:53-07:00","id":683890,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Piff</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/562137-pangea-and-the-ki-en-gir?p=562242#post562242\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As odd as this sounds, the Brineborn ought to be iterations more influential and well-known in ancient Sumeria.<br /> <br /> It'd be interesting if this was reflected - would the Forsaken be comfortable with a history which paints them as the inferiors to the FISH SHIFTERS of all folks? But seriously, the Ki En Gir had a vast cultural respect for Brineborn which was serious enough that actual Sumerian religion is largely based upon the idea of fish-people mystics with sagelike powers emerging from the deep.<br /> <br /> I have a question! Are these Border Marches mentioned in other gamelines I'm unfamiliar with, like Changeling or Mage?</div> </div> </div> </div>Those who like Dagon &amp; Deep One resonant weirdness should be quite tickled by this. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-30T21:31:31-07:00","id":683929,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/562137-pangea-and-the-ki-en-gir?p=683858#post683858\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That does have some implications I hadn't thought of before: the Exarchs, at the very least, are Supernal symbols of tyranny and oppression, which is half of what the Deceived temakhs are, at the least</div> </div> </div> </div>If I recall correctly, the Shan'iatu where put in the world to be mentors and teachers. Fitting them into Supernal symbols of tyranny and oppression from the get-go creates issues considering their present state is a result of their own screw up.<br /> <br /> One certainly helps amplify the other but I would be hesitant to say they are Supernal symbols of tyranny and oppression else you need to start including beings such as the Kindred into that mix as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-30T22:08:13-07:00","id":683943,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/562137-pangea-and-the-ki-en-gir?p=683304#post683304\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Unfortunately, one of the things the Neolithic Era <i>does</i> have in it, along with the crossover sidebar talking about how the Shan'iatu haven't built Irem yet, is an Exarch.<br /> <br /> It's pre-Sundering, not pre-Fall. The Exarchs already ruled the supernal while the Shan'iatu were building up to their project in the Sahara.</div> </div> </div> </div> Well, the Exarchs have <i>always</i> ruled the Supernal, haven't they? At least from the point of view of the Fallen World, retroactive history rewrite and all.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/614-eolirin","name":"Eolirin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-30T22:16:03-07:00","id":683947,"title":"","content":"Keep in mind that the temakhs of the Deceived are a corruption of the Shan'iatu; broken fragments of demigods who had at times, put aside their purpose and taken advice from their enemy.<br /> <br /> @Eolirin: Yes, very much so. Supernal stuff tends to do retroactively and for always. Any changes to that would rewrite the universe and there are a number of entities that don't want that. Also called out as a reason Archmasters don't try to pull this kind of thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":1624,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","user":"FallenEco","date":". 10-01-2015, 01:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-01T04:30:23-07:00","id":684251,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/562137-pangea-and-the-ki-en-gir?p=683271#post683271\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I admit, I liked The Bird and the Bull better. :/</div> </div> </div> </div> It didn't fit quite so well with the chapter's final form. The Bull and the Bird are both still in there, though.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/562137-pangea-and-the-ki-en-gir?p=683890#post683890\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Those who like Dagon &amp; Deep One resonant weirdness should be quite tickled by this. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div> As I noted upthread, Werewolf 2e already features piscine sages <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-01T05:39:12-07:00","id":684303,"title":"","content":"Afzu\u2019Umm\u2019Ia is not Mother Ocean.<br /> Probably. Maybe.<br /> Bith Balag are not in any way an idigam plot.<br /> Move along.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-01T05:59:38-07:00","id":684340,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/562137-pangea-and-the-ki-en-gir?p=684251#post684251\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Those who like Dagon &amp; Deep One resonant weirdness should be quite tickled by this. <img src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div> </div> </div> </div>As I noted upthread, Werewolf 2e already features piscine sages <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, but what is their temper and interests like? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-01T08:52:21-07:00","id":684501,"title":"","content":"They are ill tempered, and they are interested in lasers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-01T12:39:26-07:00","id":684763,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shock</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/562137-pangea-and-the-ki-en-gir?p=683929#post683929\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I recall correctly, the Shan'iatu where put in the world to be mentors and teachers. Fitting them into Supernal symbols of tyranny and oppression from the get-go creates issues considering their present state is a result of their own screw up.<br /> <br /> One certainly helps amplify the other but I would be hesitant to say they are Supernal symbols of tyranny and oppression else you need to start including beings such as the Kindred into that mix as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>My only rationale was that their temakh Virtues include Authority, Conquest, Corruption, and Vengeance","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-03T06:18:04-07:00","id":686903,"title":"","content":"So, was Irem post-Sundering, Ki-En-Gir probably was ruled by Oa &amp; the Brineborn and the Shan'iatu are the most likely candidates for killing the Divine Fish King.<br /> <br /> Given how the character creation in Hunting Grounds: Sumar &amp; Bau, it is not unreasonable to assume that Ki-En-Gir might have relics of Pangea/the Border Marches, if we go that route.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-03T11:42:32-07:00","id":687333,"title":"","content":"I think when the Sundering happened is not set in stone. We have a few hard limits on it, by the time of the First Sothic turn it was post-Sundering, but by the Neolithic Dark Era (6th Century BC, iirc[Edit: I actually meant 6th Millennium]) it was pre-Sundering. Irem falls between these two points. In my personal game, I have the Sundering coinciding with the Rite of Return.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u><b>My Homebrew</b></u><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PLu_eTg03h4ogiTSGSkzEB7T_1YpB9_VkhHmgZN41-I/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Star Wars d10</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">T</a><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">he Fallen for Demon: the Descent</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-TDr4NF_5cUn-In2vjI9P5LTKqsu9B4-OMxbnbaTgT8/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Requiem for a Masquerade: VtR 2e Cainite Conversion</a> (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HpKi5giBNsQrZRLIRRjaCe7sHVm1Q13ravVYlE45Dbw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Vampira Roma</a>)","edited":{"userid":1601,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","user":"Dreaminggod","date":". 10-03-2015, 06:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","name":"Dreaminggod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"745"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-03T13:43:59-07:00","id":687440,"title":"","content":"The Neolithic Dark Era is 5500BC-5000BC, so a fair old bit earlier than the 6th century BC!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-03T15:38:46-07:00","id":687594,"title":"","content":"Errmmm, yeah. I meant 6th Millennium. That's what I get for typing hastily and not reading over what I wrote.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u><b>My 